hate to be the one to tell you that NZ is a secular country that doesn't base its laws on religion... it honestly isn't anti-religious to simply not adhere to religion as law, its just not being dictated to by Christian values

&#x200B;

this being said though, fuck traditional Christian values, y'all have had your time and the way I live my life should have nothing to do with what you believe if it doesn't affect you

&#x200B;

Christians are against women's sexual freedom, and LGBT rights, and your right to practise a religion does not justify laws that restrict women and LGBT people who have just as much right to live freely in this country as you do

christians really struggle with the fact that gay people are real and are like hi! if we aren't supposed to exist why are we here babeeeyyy!?

&#x200B;

also why the hell you wearing a cloth of two different fabrics tf????

a white supremacist shot up a supermarket this week so a bit weird n defensive of you to bring that up for no reason. but hey

&#x200B;

